From 0c9b728d4a10b875e67321900e597bc51a489133 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "ripmav-bot[bot]" <353694380+ripmav-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:01:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libobs: add OBS_ENABLE_RUST option (Rust leaf-module swap,
 obs-rust P1-08.5)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When OBS_ENABLE_RUST=ON, the ported leaf modules (base.c, lexer.c,
cf-lexer.c, cf-parser.c, text-lookup.c, threading-posix.c and, with GLib,
platform-nix-dbus.c / platform-nix-portal.c) are excluded from the build
and their symbols are provided by the Rust staticlib named in
OBS_RUST_FFI_LIB (cargo build -p obs-ffi --release --features c-swap).

Regenerated against the 33.0.1 pin (obs-rust D3, WP-30): the previous
patch targeted the fe1ed79 working tree; against 33.0.1 the hunk
offsets are clean. WP-30 (P1-07.3) extends the swap set with the two
Flatpak sleep-inhibition files (the six dbus_/portal_inhibit* symbols
come from the Rust staticlib; the dispatcher in platform-nix.c stays C).
Mechanism verified with a shadow CMake project (genex source exclusion
+ imported staticlib resolving the real text_lookup_create symbol); a
full libobs configure needs the complete OBS dependency set and remains
unverified here.

WP-32 (P1-14.2) extends the swap set with the serializers and the bit
reader (bitstream.c, array-serializer.c, file-serializer.c,
buffered-file-serializer.c — their EXPORT symbols come from the Rust
staticlib; serializer.h, darray.h and deque.h stay C headers whose
inline code drives the Rust state).

WP-37 (P1-12.3) extends the swap set with the source profiler
(source-profiler.c — S-055 U3; the 15 source_profiler_* symbols come
from the Rust staticlib, source-profiler.h stays the C header) and adds
util/srcprof-bridge.c, the profiler bridge's graphics-context shim
(obs->video.graphics enter/leave — compiled into libobs when the Rust
staticlib provides the profiler; the conformance swap runner compiles
the identical copy from crates/obs-ffi/c/).

WP-43 (P1-01.3) extends the swap set with util/bmem.c (the six bmem
symbols — bmalloc, brealloc, bfree, bmemdup, bnum_allocs,
base_get_alignment — come from the Rust staticlib; the Rust allocator's
fatal paths route through the C bcrash shim, so crash behaviour is
unchanged). The whole swap build shares the single Rust allocator from
here on: any build that links the staticlib must drop every swapped C
source (duplicate symbols).

WP-43 (P1-15.4/P1-16.5/P1-17.4/P1-18.4) extends the swap set with the
nine exported graphics math files (graphics/{vec3,vec4,quat,axisang,
matrix3,matrix4,plane,bounds,math-extra}.c — the 80 EXPORT symbols
 come from the Rust staticlib; vec2.c stays, its helpers
are static inline in vec2.h; matrix4_mul_4x3_only has no header
declaration and is dropped with the file).

Assisted-by: Qwen3.8-27B (off) via pi
---
